our, and acute myeloid leukemia, I'm starting to mark out the span boundaries for \"juvenile granulosa cell tumour.\"\n\nI'm leaning toward DiseaseClass for mesothelioma since it covers multiple specific subtypes, while desmoplastic small round cell tumour and acute myeloid leukemia read as specific diseases. I'm now working through the exact character offsets for each disease mention across these sentences, verifying span boundaries like \"childhood kidney cancer\" (122-145), \"Wilms tumour\" (148-160), \"WT\" (163-165), \"Denys-Drash syndrome\" (387-407), and the later list of tumour types (558-705), double-checking each by counting characters from known anchor points in the text. I decide these list items like the mesothelioma and tumour types should be annotated as separate individual disease mentions rather than one composite span, since the \"most recently\" interjection breaks contiguity.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":122,\"end\":145,\"text\":\"childhood kidney cancer\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Descriptive name used in apposition with Wilms tumour, referring to one specific disease (Wilms tumour) rather than a family of diseases.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions; 6. Annotate all synonymous mentions\"},{\"start\":148,\"end\":160,\"text\":\"Wilms tumour\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Named specific childhood kidney tumour that maps to one definition without further subcategorization.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions\"},{\"start\":163,\"end\":165,\"text\":\"WT\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Abbreviation for Wilms tumour, annotated as a separate synonymous mention from the long form.\",\"guideline_section\":\"6. Annotate all synonymous mentions\"},{\"start\":313,\"end\":326,\"text\":\"Wilms tumours\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Plural mention of the specific disease Wilms tumour; the